A generic method forwards its type variable to an overloaded method.
```java
public class P2160 {
    static class A { String f(Object o) { return "obj"; } String f(String s) { return "str"; } }
    static <T> String pick(T t, A a) { return a.f(t); }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        A a = new A();
        System.out.println(pick("x", a) + ":" + pick((Object) "x", a));
    }
}
```
